      "writtenOn": "2017-02-21T07:34:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "it still needs to zero the top 32-bit word of the u64 (before returning it).\n\nGCC does the following, it\u0027s only half-stupid :\n(it has 4 useless/no-op instructions: movs\tr3, #0 / movs\tr5, #0 / orrs\tr1, r3 / orrs\tr1, r5)\n00000000 \u003cload_3\u003e:\n   0:\tb5f0      \tpush\t{r4, r5, r6, r7, lr}\n   2:\t7846      \tldrb\tr6, [r0, #1]\n   4:\t7804      \tldrb\tr4, [r0, #0]\n   6:\t0232      \tlsls\tr2, r6, #8\n   8:\t7886      \tldrb\tr6, [r0, #2]\n   a:\t2300      \tmovs\tr3, #0\n   c:\t0430      \tlsls\tr0, r6, #16\n   e:\t2100      \tmovs\tr1, #0\n  10:\t2500      \tmovs\tr5, #0\n  12:\t4310      \torrs\tr0, r2\n  14:\t4319      \torrs\tr1, r3\n  16:\t4320      \torrs\tr0, r4\n  18:\t4329      \torrs\tr1, r5\n  1a:\tbdf0      \tpop\t{r4, r5, r6, r7, pc}\nThe more aggressive LLVM optimization works properly.\n\nThe slowdown being minimum and the goal being to keep the validated code as-is, I will probably let it this way.",
